C/ CANCEL of a cyclic task that is still DORMANT (scheduled REPEAT EVERY,
C/ but CANCELed before it ever initiates) -- USA003087 Sec. 23.6 / class-0/
C/ CANC.md's "no effect unless not-yet-initiated": the not-yet-initiated
C/ task is removed and never runs.  Non-preemptive scheduling means A does
C/ not run between the SCHEDULE and the immediately-following CANCEL, so A
C/ never executes at all.  Expected: BEFORE / DONE (no "IN A").
 TCANCEL: PROGRAM;
    A: TASK;
       WRITE(6) 'IN A';
    CLOSE A;
    WRITE(6) 'BEFORE';
    SCHEDULE A PRIORITY(80), REPEAT EVERY 1.0;
    CANCEL A;
    WAIT 1.0;
    WRITE(6) 'DONE';
 CLOSE TCANCEL;
